cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the version-specific Zenodo dataset release used in your analysis."
type: dataset
title: "Global Ocean Economy Governance IGO Attribute Dataset and Reproducibility Archive"
authors:
  - family-names: "Adewumi"
    given-names: "Ibukun"
    affiliation: "Australian National Centre for Ocean Resources and Security (ANCORS), University of Wollongong"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/ADD-VERIFIED-ORCID"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
abstract: >-
  Data, documentation, coding frameworks, Python and R scripts, validation
  records, and analytical outputs supporting a comparative assessment of 48
  globally mandated intergovernmental organisations involved in global ocean
  economy governance. The archive documents governance-theme and attribute
  development, evidence-linked institutional coding, hybrid scoring, dual
  normalisation, and analyses of fragmentation, relational coordination, and
  functional differentiation.
keywords:
  - "global ocean governance"
  - "ocean economy"
  - "intergovernmental organisations"
  - "institutional design"
  - "organisational ecology"
  - "regime complexity"
  - "governance attributes"
  - "institutional fragmentation"
  - "coordination"
  - "content analysis"
  - "reproducible research"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
